Intended use: research only. Nothing radiarch produces is for clinical
use. Every result carries that statement (see README.md, "Intended use").

This product includes or runs software developed by others:

- OpenTPS core, https://gitlab.com/openmcsquare/opentps, Apache License 2.0.
  A copy is vendored under src/opentps/ with radiarch's patches recorded in
  src/opentps/patches/ and the procedure in src/opentps/ATTRIBUTION.md.
  Parts of radiarch are adapted from it.

- MCsquare, https://gitlab.com/openmcsquare/MCsquare, Apache License 2.0.
  Binaries, material tables, beam data libraries and scanner calibration
  tables are shipped under src/opentps/core/processing/doseCalculation/
  protons/MCsquare/ and are run as separate processes. radiarch's driver
  for the engine's file protocol (services/dose_engines/mcsquare_driver.py)
  is a port of OpenTPS's mcsquareIO.py and mcsquareDoseCalculator.py, and
  services/dose_engines/mcsquare_config_template.txt is the engine's
  configuration template as shipped with OpenTPS core.

- WiscPlan collapsed-cone photon dose engine (CCC_DoseEngine), GNU General
  Public License version 2, shipped as source and a prebuilt Linux binary
  under src/opentps/core/processing/doseCalculation/photons/. radiarch runs
  it only as a separate program that exchanges files with it; nothing in
  radiarch links to or imports it.

- Test data: the SimpleFantomWithStruct DICOM set from the OpenTPS test data.
